cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Measuring dependency promotion in conversational AI: reliability of a
  scenario-based multi-judge instrument
message: If you use this instrument, data or code, please cite the paper.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Kadakia
    given-names: Arya
abstract: >-
  A scenario-based benchmark for dependency-promoting behaviour in conversational
  AI, with a reliability analysis of the instrument. Agreement between raters
  tracks how often a behaviour occurs, so most of the dimensions that discriminate
  between models are ones two consistent raters do not agree on.
keywords:
  - conversational AI
  - AI safety
  - inter-rater reliability
  - LLM-as-judge
  - digital health
  - human-AI interaction
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: '2026-09-16'
